          "details": {
            "answer": "TCP opens a connection with a three‑way handshake:\n\n1. **SYN** – The client sends a segment with the SYN flag set and an initial sequence number (ISN) to the server.  \n2. **SYN‑ACK** – The server replies with a segment that has both SYN and ACK flags set; it includes its own ISN and acknowledges the client’s ISN.  \n3. **ACK** – The client sends a final ACK segment acknowledging the server’s ISN.  \n\nAfter this exchange the connection is established and data can be transferred[[1]].",
            "citations": 1
          }
