          "details": {
            "answer": "Before the Revolution, French society was organized into three distinct estates. The First Estate comprised the clergy, the Second Estate the nobility, and the Third Estate included everyone else—by far the largest group, which bore most of the tax burden while the clergy and nobles enjoyed extensive privileges[1].",
            "citations": 1
